  30:Core/Src/startup.c ****     - Linker script variables add the variableName to the symbol table and the
  31:Core/Src/startup.c ****     value that the variable is assigned to, is stored in an entry with the variableName 
  32:Core/Src/startup.c ****     in the symbol table(so the value that the variableName is assigned to is its address not value)
  33:Core/Src/startup.c ****     typically for declarations in C in symbol table you would store varName = memory address of val
  34:Core/Src/startup.c ****     but with a linker script variable there is no memory assigned to the variable
  35:Core/Src/startup.c ****     - This is why in source code you access &_startDataRAM and same for other linker 
  36:Core/Src/startup.c ****     script variables because all you want is the address of the variable because the value of 
