  38:Core/Src/startup.c ****     - using the value of a variable in source code(so if you have
  39:Core/Src/startup.c ****     int a = 5; int b = a + 2) will get address of a from symbol table and use the 
  40:Core/Src/startup.c ****     address to get the value of a 
  41:Core/Src/startup.c ****     - So plainly using _startDataRam will cause problems because there is no memory
  42:Core/Src/startup.c ****     assigned to _startDataRam so you can't access a value like you typically would for 
  43:Core/Src/startup.c ****     high level variables
